[9014]={o="Give Mokvar your Magister's Crown and Magister's Robes.",d="A truly amazing story, <name>! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\n\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.",p="As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Magister's pieces in exchange for your new Sorcerer's Crown and Robes?",c="I will truly miss you, <name>. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\n\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!",r={it={{22065,1,"Sorcerer's Crown",4,"inv_crown_02"},{22069,1,"Sorcerer's Robes",4,"inv_chest_cloth_25"}}},k=true},
[9015]={o="Travel to the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths and place the Banner of Provocation in its center as you are sentenced by High Justice Grimstone.  Slay Theldren and his gladiators and return to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands with the first piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet.",d="Heed me well, <name>.  For the banner to work in the desired way, you will need to step into the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths.  Allow yourself to be sentenced by High Justice Grimstone and place the banner firmly on the ground in a sign of defiance.\n\nYour victim will not be able to restrain himself and shall enter the fray filled with a desire to fight you.  Once you obtain that which you seek, go back to Anthion.",p="You're back, <name>!",c="You've recovered part of the medallion, <name>?",k=true},
[9016]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22107,1,"Feralheart Boots",4,"inv_boots_08"},{22111,1,"Feralheart Kilt",3,"inv_pants_08"},{22112,1,"Feralheart Spaulders",3,"inv_shoulder_01"}}},k=true},
[9017]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Beaststalker's Boots, Beaststalker's Pants and Beaststalker's Mantle.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22061,1,"Beastmaster's Boots",4,"inv_boots_plate_07"},{22017,1,"Beastmaster's Pants",3,"inv_pants_03"},{22016,1,"Beastmaster's Mantle",3,"inv_shoulder_10"}}},k=true},
[9018]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Magister's Boots, Magister's Leggings and Magister's Mantle.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22064,1,"Sorcerer's Boots",4,"inv_boots_02"},{22067,1,"Sorcerer's Leggings",3,"inv_pants_06"},{22068,1,"Sorcerer's Mantle",3,"inv_shoulder_23"}}},k=true},
[9019]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Devout Sandals, Devout Skirt and Devout Mantle.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22084,1,"Virtuous Sandals",4,"inv_boots_05"},{22085,1,"Virtuous Skirt",3,"inv_pants_08"},{22082,1,"Virtuous Mantle",3,"inv_shoulder_02"}}},k=true},
[9020]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of  Shadowcraft Boots, Shadowcraft Pants and Shadowcraft Spaulders.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22003,1,"Darkmantle Boots",4,"inv_boots_08"},{22007,1,"Darkmantle Pants",3,"inv_pants_02"},{22008,1,"Darkmantle Spaulders",3,"inv_shoulder_07"}}},k=true},
[9021]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Dreadmist Sandals, Dreadmist Leggings and Dreadmist Mantle.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>.  Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{22076,1,"Deathmist Sandals",4,"inv_boots_05"},{22072,1,"Deathmist Leggings",3,"inv_pants_08"},{22073,1,"Deathmist Mantle",3,"inv_misc_bone_taurenskull_01"}}},k=true},
[9022]={o="Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Boots of Valor, Legplates of Valor and Spaulders of Valor.",d="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\n\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\n\nI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",p="You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, <name>. Let us take care of your reward first.",c="This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\n\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.",r={it={{21995,1,"Boots of Heroism",4,"inv_boots_plate_03"},{22000,1,"Legplates of Heroism",3,"inv_pants_04"},{22001,1,"Spaulders of Heroism",3,"inv_shoulder_30"}}},k=true},
[9023]={o="Dirk Thunderwood at Cenarion Hold wants you to bring him Venoxis's Venom Sac and Kurinnaxx's Venom Sac.",d="My brother and I run the poison operations out of the manor Ravenholdt.\n\nLord Ravenholdt tasked me to track down a new and extremely effective poison compound that can be crafted from the venom sacs of the inhabitants of Zul'Gurub and the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj.\n\nThere are two particularly venomous beasts residing in those blasted ruins that possess what it is that we might be looking for, <class>. Bring me a venom sac from the beasts Kurinnaxx and Venoxis and we would be eternally grateful.",p="This ain't no smash and grab job, <name>. You're gonna need to bring friends.",c="Ravenholdt thanks you, hero! Take your pick!",r={ch={{22378,1,"Ravenholdt Slicer",3,"inv_sword_38"},{22379,1,"Shivsprocket's Shiv",3,"inv_sword_21"},{22377,1,"The Thunderwood Poker",3,"inv_sword_17"},{22348,1,"Doomulus Prime",3,"inv_hammer_10"},{22347,1,"Fahrad's Reloading Repeater",3,"inv_weapon_crossbow_04"},{22380,1,"Simone's Cultivating Hammer",3,"inv_hammer_05"}},rep={{609,250}}},k=true},
[9032]={o="Travel to Blackrock Mountain and use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer to find Bodley near Blackrock Spire.",d="The medallion contained Valthalak's soul?  It's no surprise it was guarded by such a powerful curse.\n\nLocating Bodley presents a bit of a problem.  Last time I heard of him, he was preparing to venture back into Blackrock Spire.  He was never heard of again.\n\nSeek him out in Blackrock Mountain, though I'm afraid to say he's probably dead by now.  I suggest taking the goblin's device with you, friend.",c="I am so glad that you can see me. Finally someone to talk to!\n\nWill you help us, <name>? Help to undo the wrong that we perpetrated and put things to right? If it's true that you already have the Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet, then I think I can point you in the right direction to acquire the other two parts, reunite them and put an end to all of this.\n\nOh, by the way, hello, my name is Bodley. Nice to meet you!",k=true},
[9033]={o="Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to slay 5 Living Monstrosities, 5 Stoneskin Gargoyles, 8 Deathknight Captains and 3 Venom Stalkers.",n={{"Deathknight Captain",8},{"Venom Stalker",3},{"Living Monstrosity",5},{"Stoneskin Gargoyle",5}},d="Five years since the last war...\n\nTens of thousands of lives were lost and for what? The threat was never fully extinguished.\n\nAnd so the Lich King stirs once more... His yes-man, Kel'Thuzad, amassing for another attack upon our lands.\n\nWe will not allow it! Prove your dedication. Prove that you are willing to risk life and limb to stop this madness and the combined might of the Dawn and the Crusade will be at your beck and call.\n\nEnter Naxxramas and destroy the Scourge within...",p="Duty, honor, dedication... What do these words mean to you?",c="A job well done! You will be rewarded via the services of the men and women at Light's Hope.",k=true},
[9051]={o="Stab a Devilsaur with the Devilsaur Barb. Return to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater when you have completed this task.",d="The toxin you helped me create is for a special purpose.  The great devilsaurs of the crater make it dangerous to hunt and difficult for me to survive.  Even if I possessed the necessary strength, killing a devilsaur simply allows another to move into its territory.\n\nTake this poisoned barb and stab it deep into a living devilsaur.  The toxin should pacify the creature, though I do not know how quickly...",p="Were you able to pacify the great beast?",c="Thank you, <name>.  You are brave and wise.\n\nTell me, how did the devilsaur react to the toxin?",k=true},
[9052]={o="Collect 8 Bloodcap and 8 Gorishi Stings, and return to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.",n={{"Gorishi Sting",8},{"Bloodcap",8}},d="I would ask you to help me create a toxin of sorts, to pacify a great creature living here in the crater.  It is not deadly, and only the keen eyes of a <class> can hope to collect the ingredients.\n\nYou can find the bloodcap mushrooms growing within the bloodpetal sprouts all across the crater.  Gorishi stings are from the insects inside and around the Slithering Scar, located in the southern part of the crater.",p="Have you met with success?",c="The ingredients at last!\n\nWith the Un'Goro soil I have collected, the toxin is easily concocted...",r={it={{13446,2,"Major Healing Potion",1,"inv_potion_54"}}},k=true},
[9053]={o="Retrieve a Putrid Vine from the guardian at the bottom of the Sunken Temple and return to Torwa Pathfinder.",d="It is as I feared -- the toxin is simply too weak for such a powerful creature.\n\nIf we are to create a toxin of high enough potency, you must venture to the bottom of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, unlock the secrets of the altar and recover a putrid vine from the guardian there.  The temple is dangerous, and it would behoove you to bring friends.\n\nReturn to me when this is done.",p="Have you recovered the vine?",c="At last, the toxin can be created in full. I dare not require you to inflict it upon the creature again, as I have asked too much already.\n\nYou have my thanks and respect. May you be well in your travels, <name>.",r={ch={{22274,1,"Grizzled Pelt",3,"inv_chest_leather_08"},{22272,1,"Forest's Embrace",3,"inv_chest_leather_08"},{22458,1,"Moonshadow Stave",3,"inv_staff_28"}}},k=true},
[9063]={o="Speak with Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.",d="A hunter by the name of Torwa Pathfinder has requested the help of a druid.  He said only we would possess the necessary skills and respect for nature to help him.\n\nThere is a road that connects the Un'Goro Crater and the desert of Tanaris.  As that road enters the crater, you will find Torwa close by.",c="You have traveled far to meet with me, <class>, and not a moment too soon.",k=true},
[9120]={o="Take the Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad to Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",d="The phylactery is all that remains of the master of Naxxramas. Your better judgment dictates that you destroy the phylactery, preventing the lich from ever reforming. Thankfully, you seldom listen to that internal voice of reason.\n\nSomeone at Light's Hope will pay you hugely for this artifact. Who cares if Kel'Thuzad regenerates to full power?",r={ch={{23206,1,"Mark of the Champion",4,"inv_misc_token_argentdawn2"},{23207,1,"Mark of the Champion",4,"inv_misc_token_argentdawn3"}}},k=true},
[9121]={o="Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Arcane Crystals, 2 Nexus Crystals, 1 Righteous Orb and 60 gold pieces. You must also be Honored with the Argent Dawn.",n={{"Arcane Crystal",5},{"Nexus Crystal",2}},d="In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\n\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via arcane cloaking - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. Since your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is somewhat lacking, <name>, the price will be high. You may decline and choose to return when you are revered or exalted for a discount.",p="None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.",c="You will feel a slight tingle, <name>. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.",r={rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9122]={o="Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 2 Arcane Crystals, 1 Nexus Crystal and 30 gold pieces. You must also be Revered with the Argent Dawn.",n={{"Arcane Crystal",2}},d="In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\n\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via a permanent arcane cloaking of sorts - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. With that said, the cloaking is costly. Since your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is admirable, we are willing to incur some of those costs.",p="None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.",c="You will feel a slight tingle, <name>. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.",r={rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9123]={o="Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will grant you Arcane Cloaking at no cost. You must be Exalted with the Argent Dawn.",d="In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\n\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via a permanent arcane cloaking of sorts - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. With that said, the cloaking is costly; however, your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is unwavering! We will waive all cost associations.",p="None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.",c="You will feel a slight tingle, <name>. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.",k=true},
[9124]={o="Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Crypt Fiend Parts.",n={{"Crypt Fiend Parts",30}},d="How would you like to earn yourself one of these shiny coins?\n\n<Leopold holds up an insignia of the Crusade.>\n\nI've got a little problem that you might be able to help me with, <name>. You see, I make Cryptstalker armor for those daft enough to venture into Naxxramas. While they supply me with the core material requirements for the armor, I always run out of the crypt fiend parts. Bring me back a bundle of parts and I'll pay you with an insignia - usable at the quartermaster.",p="How goes the hunt?",c="Ah, that'll do nicely, <name>. Remember, I'm always accepting more parts. For every bundle you bring me, I'll reward you with an insignia.",r={it={{22524,1,"Insignia of the Crusade",2,"inv_misc_token_scarletcrusade"}},rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9126]={o="Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Bone Fragments.",n={{"Bone Fragments",30}},d="Don Julio's Bonescythe armor pattern requires bone fragments - a lot of bone fragments. While those crazy enough to venture into Naxxramas provide me with enough of the core materials to make the armor, I'm always looking for more Scourge bone fragments.\n\nSo what do you think? Interested in getting your hands dirty and destroying some Scourge at the same time? It's a win-win situation.",p="I can direct you to skeleton infested locales, <class>.",c="You work fast, <name>. Fast like a fox... Say, have I ever told you about the time I was in a barber shop quartet?\n\nRemind me to tell you that story one of these days.",r={it={{22524,1,"Insignia of the Crusade",2,"inv_misc_token_scarletcrusade"}},rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9128]={o="Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Core of Elements.",n={{"Core of Elements",30}},d="Greetings, adventurer! Are you interested in some work? I pay those under my employ with insignias. These insignias can be used at the Quartermaster to purchase items of power.\n\nAll I need you to do is bring me as many core of elements as you can carry. The more the better!\n\nYou'll find them on elementals of varying shapes and sizes that exist across our world.",p="I can only steer you in the right direction, <name>.",c="A job well done, <name>! As promised, the INsignia is yours. Just remember, there's more WHERE that came from...",r={it={{22523,1,"Insignia of the Dawn",2,"inv_misc_token_argentdawn"}},rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9131]={o="Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Dark Iron Scraps.",n={{"Dark Iron Scraps",30}},d="Have you ever seen Dreadnaught armor, <class>? No, of course you haven't. You're still a boy/girl - a tyke. Let me tell you, it is glorious.\n\nYou're probably asking yourself what any of this has to do with you, right? I'll tell you what, scrub; I need Dark Iron scraps and I'm willing to pay to get my hands on as many as possible.\n\nI need the scraps to put together sets of Dreadnaught for our champions. Bring me scraps and get paid.",p="<Korfax growls at you.>\n\nWhat do you want? Directions? I can provide those...",c="This will do, for now. If you get more, you know where to find me.",r={it={{22523,1,"Insignia of the Dawn",2,"inv_misc_token_argentdawn"}},rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9136]={o="Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Savage Fronds.",n={{"Savage Frond",30}},d="I make a special type of armor for the brave heroes that enter Naxxramas known as Dreamwalker. They are able to provide me with most of the materials I require but I am always looking for those able to retrieve savage fronds from the flora of our world.\n\nYou may think of this job as beneath you, but without the fronds, the armor could not be made.\n\nI am also in a unique position to pay you with an insignia of your choice as both the Dawn and the Crusade supply me with funds.",p="I have intimate knowledge of the flora in our world. Do you require direction?",c="I am much obliged, <name>.\n\n<Rayne bows.>\n\nPlease remember that I am always acceptINg fronds.",r={ch={{22524,1,"Insignia of the Crusade",2,"inv_misc_token_scarletcrusade"},{22523,1,"Insignia of the Dawn",2,"inv_misc_token_argentdawn"}},rep={{529,200}}},k=true},
[9141]={o="Dispatch Commander Metz at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants an Argent Dawn Valor Token.",d="You want a writ? What? Do you expect me to hand you a highly sought after work order just for showing up? I think not, scrub. Crafters from around the world bid for jobs here at the front lines.\n\nIf you want a work order, you'll have to show me that you're willing to bleed for the cause. Bring me a valor token and we'll talk.\n\nAnd there's only one way to get your grubby little scrub mitts on those - get to killin'.",p="<Commander Metz chews on his cigar.>\n\nWhat is it? I'm a busy man.",c="Alright, here's how it works: For every valor token that you turn in, I'll give you another writ. You complete the order on that writ and deliver the order to Packmaster Stonebruiser. Got it? Good. Now get out of here.",r={it={{22568,1,"Sealed Craftsman's Writ",1,"inv_scroll_04"}},rep={{529,500}}},k=true},
[9229]={o="Enter Naxxramas and uncover the Fate of Ramaladni.",d="Ramaladni was a warrior of the Brotherhood - a pupil of Highlord Mograine before the Dawn even existed! When news of Mograine's death reached him, hatred and anger took over.\n\nUnderstand this, <name>, when rage and retribution take the reins, a man ceases to be a man. The man personifies the emotions that control him instead. And so it would be that Ramaladni, the spirit of retribution, would enter Naxxramas to exact vengeance... and never return.\n\nEnter Naxxramas and find what became of Ramaladni.",p="Any news of Ramaladni?",c="It is his ring! But it is destroyed. No other evidence of Ramaladni was found?\n\n<Korfax grimaces.>\n\nThis does not bode well for Ramaladni. The ring, however... it might be salvageable.",k=true},
[9230]={o="Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to bring him 1 Frozen Rune, 1 Blue Sapphire and 1 Arcanite Bar.",d="Fixing this band may prove to be quite challenging, <name>. You see, it was made from the very runes that form inside Scourge structures - like Naxxramas. Additional materials are also required but your main concern should be getting those frozen runes. Bring me what I need and I will restore the ring to its former glory.",p="Frozen runes could probably be found inside Naxxramas.",c="Ramaladni himself couldn't have done better! Here is the ring, as promised.",r={it={{22707,1,"Ramaladni's Icy Grasp",4,"inv_jewelry_ring_35"}}},k=true},
[9232]={o="Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to bring him 2 Frozen Runes, 2 Essence of Water, 2 Blue Sapphires and 30 gold pieces.",n={{"Frozen Rune",2},{"Essence of Water",2},{"Blue Sapphire",2}},d="You fancy yourself a hero of the Dawn, eh? I've seen our greatest soldiers get rolled over by Kel'Thuzad's plebes! How well could someone so clueless possibly fare in Naxxramas?\n\n<Wilhelm sighs.>\n\nBah, what choice do I got? You're the best I can do; I may as well help you.\n\nOmarion left me with one recipe. It's the only song I know... I can make a few variations of these pants; you just gotta supply the materials.",p="You haven't run into Omarion, have you?",c="<Wilhelm wipes the sweat from his brow.>\n\nThat's some hard work! Enjoy the pants, <class>. At least you'll die in a clean pair now.",r={ch={{22700,1,"Glacial Leggings",4,"inv_pants_06"},{22699,1,"Icebane Leggings",4,"inv_pants_04"},{22702,1,"Icy Scale Leggings",4,"inv_pants_mail_15"},{22701,1,"Polar Leggings",4,"inv_pants_leather_21"}}},k=true},
[9233]={o="Take Omarion's Handbook to Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",d="Wilhelm,\n\nIf you are reading this, I have perished - finally. I want you to know that my dying thoughts revolved around you and your ineptitude when it comes to tradeskills. Unfortunately, the bearer of this handbook is in even worse shape than you in regards to crafting.\n\nAbout the book: These are the rest of my recipes. Make the bearer of this book whatever they request. I'm sure you will charge a hefty fee for your services because you are, after all, a bastard.\n\nIn Disdain,\n\nOmarion",p="Is that what I think it is?\n\n<Wilhelm appears to be drooling.>",c="He musta really been off his rocker when he wrote this! Omarion and I - we were thick as thieves!\n\nAnyhow, this certainly opens up some new possibilities, <name>. I am now able to craft more items - for a small fee and material charges, of course.",k=true},
[9234]={o="Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essences of Water and 200 gold.",n={{"Frozen Rune",5},{"Thorium Bar",12},{"Arcanite Bar",2},{"Essence of Water",2}},d="Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create Icebane gauntlets. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.",p="Have you brought the materials?",c="Here is your order, <name>. Delivered as promised!",r={it={{22670,1,"Icebane Gauntlets",4,"inv_gauntlets_28"}}},k=true},
[9235]={o="Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essence of Water and 200 gold.",n={{"Frozen Rune",4},{"Thorium Bar",12},{"Arcanite Bar",2},{"Essence of Water",2}},d="Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create Icebane bracers. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.",p="Have you brought the materials?",c="Here is your order, <name>. Delivered as promised!",r={it={{22671,1,"Icebane Bracers",4,"inv_bracer_07"}}},k=true},
[9236]={o="Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 16 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 4 Essence of Water and 300 gold. You will also need to be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",n={{"Frozen Rune",8},{"Thorium Bar",16},{"Arcanite Bar",2},{"Essence of Water",4}},d="Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create an Icebane breastplate. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.",p="Have you brought the materials?",c="Here is your order, <name>. Delivered as promised!",r={it={{22669,1,"Icebane Breastplate",4,"inv_chest_chain_11"}}},k=true},
[9237]={o="Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 2 Essences of Water, 4 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.",n={{"Frozen Rune",5},{"Bolt of Runecloth",4},{"Essence of Water",2},{"Ironweb Spider Silk",4}},d="Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create a Glacial cloak. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.",p="Have you brought the materials?",c="Here is your order, <name>. Delivered as promised!",r={it={{22658,1,"Glacial Cloak",4,"inv_misc_cape_16"}}},k=true},
